le>Rocket from Boeing-Lockheed firm fails mid-flight, destroys payload of Amazon satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da95e730014214984e6f587f48ca1300c1ba34c56c5a382c2f32b0e1e61ce1bc</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:51:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T04:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rocket-from-boeing-lockheed-firm-fails-mid-flight-destroys-payload-of-amazon-satellites/a-79953931--2246e96a9407.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rocket-from-boeing-lockheed-firm-fails-mid-flight-destroys-payload-of-amazon-satellites/a-79953931?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Vulcan rocket suffered an anomaly about 10 minutes after liftoff from Florida, failing to deliver 40 Amazon Leo satellites to orbit. It was the first total mission failure in the company's history.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Anti-Houthi forces pull back as rebels advance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16951ba3613ffbc453c5e14ccb41def618047fe03eb520da5e5117cea5e72823</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:51:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T23:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-anti-houthi-forces-pull-back-as-rebels-advance/a-79953692--bce2a6257bd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-anti-houthi-forces-pull-back-as-rebels-advance/a-79953692?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Forces aligned with the Yemeni government and Saudi Arabia are seeking to strengthen control over the interim capital Aden as the Iran-backed Houthis approach.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Goodbye, overtourism? Sustainable travel gains ground</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07ebf4e3f9e7ae2b469a82c8bcf3b957842fb8834cd07c6a16443e15a6ff5056</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:49:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T20:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/goodbye-overtourism-community-based-travel-gaining-ground/a-79934295--d0f6211a9dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/goodbye-overtourism-sustainable-travel-gains-ground/a-79934295?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As tourism booms across Latin America, alternative forms of travel are gaining ground. Making your holiday more sustainable means rethinking who calls the shots, who invests and who benefits.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy urges removal of Starshield limits on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92fba43d49667919ae3891d3a1a2c81762b147eea913a527bae290839b5daaab</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:49:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T20:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-urges-removal-of-starshield-limits-on-ukraine/a-79953300--505b8186cf0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-urges-removal-of-starshield-limits-on-ukraine/a-79953300?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's government has said the throttling of satellite-based internet system prevents Kyiv from intercepting Russian attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia: Scores protest against public media reform</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f90bf22b12c6627967f8f491efd9d319f39dbc00dc13b2aaf9509ff18e22403e</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:49:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T19:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-scores-protest-against-public-media-reform/a-79953057--804bd6cc316f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-scores-protest-against-public-media-reform/a-79953057?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of people gathered to protest against the government's plan to abolish broadcasting fees. Critics say the nationalist coalition would like to secure control over the media.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Estonia closes border to Russia after suspected drone factory arson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26d4bf44bbbbd4787c95ed2dd22b2ed9bd9ea1537250d7bddc22588305296b63</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:49:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/estonia-closes-border-to-russia-after-suspected-drone-factory-arson/a-79953115--0e59b4bde9de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/estonia-closes-border-to-russia-after-suspected-drone-factory-arson/a-79953115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tallinn has accused Russia of conducting hybrid warfare after a drone factory was set alight in Viimsi. Now it will close its border crossings at the start of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nearly 1,600 migrants arrive on Spain's Canary Islands in one day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e699fb563c26a99c46aac05f89b6f1bd7d3c1a42aa56982c26eab98c73ec9bf</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:49:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941--709bffa2c1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The majority of the migrants who arrived on the islands on Saturday came from Senegal, Gambia, and Guinea. The surge in arrivals to the Canaries comes after Spain's Ceuta recently faced a migration crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cape Verde election: Jose Maria Neves set to win second term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:481a3cf15ba0efdc27d3d59f86792bce1d4737060748b0c05c1a5711bcbb35fb</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:51:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate"